========================================================================
PART E.2 - CARDINALITY EXPLOSION
========================================================================
A counter labelled with request_id creates ONE NEW TIME SERIES PER
REQUEST. Capped at 100 distinct ids, as the assignment requires.

[0] preparing
  -> restarting storefront-api with CARDINALITY_DEMO_LABEL=request_id
     storefront-api is back up (label mode: request_id)

[1] before - demo counter not yet written
     count(demo_requests_total)          : 0
     series stored in the last 10 minutes : 0
     count(demo_requests_safe_total)      : 0
     TSDB head series (whole Prometheus)  : 2820

[2] demo_requests_total{request_id=...} - the unbounded label
  -> sending 100 requests, each with a fresh request id
     count(demo_requests_total)          : 100
     series stored in the last 10 minutes : 100
     count(demo_requests_safe_total)      : 0
     TSDB head series (whole Prometheus)  : 3056

[3] label removed from the code, app restarted, same test repeated
  -> restarting storefront-api with CARDINALITY_DEMO_LABEL=none
     storefront-api is back up (label mode: none)
  -> sending 100 requests, each with a fresh request id
     count(demo_requests_total)          : 1
     series stored in the last 10 minutes : 101
     count(demo_requests_safe_total)      : 0
     TSDB head series (whole Prometheus)  : 3077

[4] extra: a bounded label (tier = standard | vip), 100 requests
     count(demo_requests_total)          : 1
     series stored in the last 10 minutes : 101
     count(demo_requests_safe_total)      : 2
     TSDB head series (whole Prometheus)  : 3099

[5] restoring the default configuration
  -> restarting storefront-api with CARDINALITY_DEMO_LABEL=request_id
     storefront-api is back up (label mode: request_id)

========================================================================
RESULT
========================================================================
  100 requests, request_id label  -> +100 series
  100 requests, label removed     -> 1 series
  100 requests, bounded tier label -> 2 series
  but Prometheus still stored 101 distinct demo series in the last 10 minutes

  NOTE: removing the label stops NEW series being created, and the old
  ones drop out of instant queries once they go stale. Their samples
  stay on disk until retention deletes them.

  full record written to results\cardinality-20260923-192022.json

